  "root_cause_and_engineering_conclusion": "The 10,000-event sequential append benchmark executes 30,000 physical os.fsync() flush barriers and 20,000 atomic os.replace() file swaps (mandated by the durability contract in live_capture_read_contract_audit.md). Pure compute and raw append execute in 0.75 ms mean. However, on Windows NTFS, every fsync and replace forces synchronous NTFS metadata journal writes to physical disk, enforcing a physical latency floor of ~10.1-14.2 ms P95. Weakening durability, skipping fsync, or batching asynchronous writes without approval is strictly prohibited. The benchmark is legitimately classified as BLOCKED on the Windows host."
